Title: Raid prints a portable sitrep every 15 minutes
Created: 2026-10-27
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-10-27T09:55Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context

The raid has an executor-side watchdog (`raid-breaker.py`: 10-minute
stall window, gate heartbeat, `--wait` that wakes the coordinator on
`STALL`/`GATE_TIMEOUT`), but nothing on the coordinator side. An author
who steps away during a raid has no progress trail until the wrap-up
briefing, and a coordinator that went quiet is only noticed by looking.

The author asked for a sitrep every 15 minutes that works on every runtime
the harness supports (Claude Code, Codex, Pi), not just a Claude Code
session cron. A 1-minute idle nudge was considered and set aside: each
wake re-reads the coordinator's whole context (~9M cached tokens/hour at
150K context), and a coordinator with pending background work is already
woken by its notifications and by `raid-breaker.py --wait`.

## Design direction

Split what must be portable from what cannot be:

1. **Sitrep producer, runtime-agnostic.** A script (e.g.
   `scripts/raid-sitrep.py`) that renders the sitrep from durable state
   only: the raid log, git (branches, worktrees, `WAVE_BASE`), the forge's
   open PRs behind `# harness-extension-point`, and `raid-breaker.py`
   readings. Because it reads disk and forge state and no conversation, any
   runtime, the author's own shell (`watch -n 900 ...`) or a system timer can run it.
   Today the raid log has no fixed path (`skills/raid/SKILL.md` mentions it
   at the `WAVE_BASE` step), so this ticket fixes one.
2. **Wake source, per runtime, behind an extension point.** In Claude Code,
   a background command that exits on a 15-minute deadline wakes the
   coordinator, like `raid-breaker.py --wait`. Codex and Pi: find each
   runtime's equivalent; where none exists, the raid prints the sitrep at
   each wave boundary and each circuit-breaker event, and says that the
   timed cadence is unavailable on that runtime.
3. **Fold the nudge into the sitrep.** When the sitrep shows nothing in
   flight and a non-empty queue, the coordinator resumes the next wave
   rather than ending its turn.

Sitrep content (one screen): elapsed time vs. deadline/budget, current
wave and its tickets, each PR's step (executing / gaze / gate round N /
merged / escalated), breakers fired since the last sitrep, the next action.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The raid log has a fixed, documented path, and the raid writes the
      state the sitrep needs into it.
- [ ] `scripts/raid-sitrep.py` renders the sitrep from durable state alone
      and exits non-zero when it could not read part of its state. It
      never prints an all-clear it cannot distinguish from "could not look".
- [ ] `skills/raid/SKILL.md` arms the 15-minute cadence at raid start and
      disarms it at wrap-up; runtime-specific lines sit behind
      `<!-- harness-extension-point -->` (`scripts/check-agnostic.sh` passes).
- [ ] The per-runtime wake source is documented for Claude Code, Codex and
      Pi. A runtime without one degrades to wave-boundary sitreps, says
      so, and does not fail silently.
- [ ] An idle coordinator with a non-empty queue resumes on the sitrep
      wake (folded nudge); one with an empty queue proceeds to wrap-up.
- [ ] Tests cover rendering from a fixture raid log, the unreadable-state
      exit, and the empty-queue vs. non-empty-queue branch.
- [ ] `make check` passes.
